W44-145 per-block adaptive qac scaling A/B — HONEST-STOP (2026-05-21)
======================================================================

Status: [HONEST-STOP — mechanism implemented + tested, NOT shipped to
production qf_pre_scale apply site; helper functions retained as
`#[allow(dead_code)]` for future use.]

Repo state:
  git rev:    pending commit (W44-145 investigation)
  ours cli:   /home/lilith/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target/release/cjxl-rs
  host:       lilith
  command:    cargo run --release --features 'butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop
              parallel' --example w44_145_per_block_qac_ab --manifest-path
              jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml

Goal (per W44-145 task spec, Phase 2 candidate 2 from W44-144 memo):
  Close the terminal e5/e6/e7 d=4 SSIM2/bytes-overhead cluster by
  routing the W44-109 adaptive_quant qf seed scale through a per-block
  mask1x1 lookup, so blank-mask blocks get scale ≈ 1.0 (keeping qac at
  baseline ~7-8) and text-mask blocks get the full per-effort scale
  (mirroring cjxl's bimodal qac at e8+ where text qac ≈ 97 and blank
  qac ≈ 7).

Acceptance gates (task spec):
  (a) SSIM2 within ±0.30 of pre-W44-145 baseline OR improved on the
      terminal d=4 primary cells (e5/e6/e7)
  (b) bytes overhead REDUCED from +33% baseline toward +10-15%
  (c) terminal e5/e6/e7 d=3.5/d=4.5 adjacent cells: bytes ±5%,
      SSIM2 ±0.10
  (d) terminal e8/e9 d=4: byte-identical (W44-105 owns qac at e>=8)
  (e) codec_wiki d=3/d=4: byte-identical (different content class)
  (f) terminal d=1.0/d=2: byte-identical or within budget
  (g) photo cells: byte-identical (is_screenshot=false)
  (h) imac_g3 d=2/d=3: byte-impact reduced, SSIM2 preserved
  (i) hash-locks 36/36 byte-identical
  (j) multi-decoder roundtrip on 1 closed cell

Mechanism (`vardct/butteraugli_loop.rs`):
  `per_block_mask1x1_mean(mask1x1, padded_width, xs_b, ys_b) -> Vec<f32>`
    — computes mean of mask1x1 per 8×8 block (length xs_b * ys_b)
  `w44_145_per_block_qf_scale(block_mask_mean, full_scale) -> f32`
    — linear interp between 1.0 (at mask >= HIGH=99.5) and full_scale
      (at mask <= LOW). Returns 1.0 when full_scale == 1.0.

  Bisected LOW thresholds:
    v1: LOW=70 (initial estimate based on W44-145 doc reference values
        — text mask 20-60, blank mask saturates ~100)
    v2: LOW=95 (conservative — only blocks in [95, 99.5] get any
        scale reduction; most blocks stay at full W44-109 scale)

Results (35 cells × 2 modes paired interleaved):

  See `w44_145_per_block_qac_ab_v1_low70_2026-05-21.tsv` and
      `w44_145_per_block_qac_ab_v2_low95_2026-05-21.tsv`

  Primary terminal d=4 cluster:

  | cell           | v1 bytes Δ | v1 SSIM2 Δ | v2 bytes Δ | v2 SSIM2 Δ |
  |----------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|
  | terminal e5 d=4| -3.04 %    | **-0.41**  | +0.63 %    | -0.07      |
  | terminal e6 d=4| -2.54 %    | -0.34      | +0.82 %    | -0.12      |
  | terminal e7 d=4| -8.53 %    | **-0.50**  | +2.73 %    | -0.16      |

  v1 FAILS gate (a) on e5 and e7 (SSIM2 < -0.30);
                FAILS gate (b) on all 3 cells (-3 to -8.5% from W44-109
                baseline = +29% to +22% overhead vs cjxl, target was +10-15%).

  v2 PASSES gate (a) on all 3 cells (SSIM2 -0.07 to -0.16, within ±0.30);
                FAILS gate (b) on all 3 cells (bytes +0.6 to +2.7% =
                WRONG DIRECTION — overhead vs cjxl went UP from +33% to
                +34% to +36%).

  W44-145 mechanism cannot satisfy gates (a) AND (b) simultaneously at
  any LOW threshold in the bisection. The fundamental obstacle:

ROOT CAUSE — cjxl is NOT bimodal at e5-e7:

  W44-144 Phase 1 dump (CLAUDE.md investigation notes 2026-05-21)
  cited cjxl's bimodal qac on terminal d=4 e8+ (text ≈ 97, blank ≈ 7).
  Re-reading the dump confirms this is e8+ ONLY (post-buttloop):

    e5 mean qac per region: cjxl 7.6 to 8.2 (FLAT)
    e7 mean qac per region: cjxl 7.7 to 9.2 (FLAT)
    e8 mean qac per region: cjxl 7.2 to 97.4 (BIMODAL)

  At e5-e7, cjxl runs a FLAT lower qac everywhere (~7-9). W44-109's
  uniform 2×/3× scale lifts our qac to 15.5-25.7 to mimic cjxl's
  byte overhead at d=4 (which itself pays bytes for fine quant
  everywhere). The W44-109 bytes overhead is the price for matching
  cjxl's SSIM2 at e5-e7.

  W44-145 attempted to be SMARTER than cjxl: scale only text blocks
  while leaving blanks coarse-quantized. But cjxl is NOT actually
  coarse-quantizing blanks at e5-e7 — it runs fine quant everywhere.
  Skipping the scale on blanks means our blanks are coarser than
  cjxl's, costing SSIM2 there without recovering enough bytes
  elsewhere to hit the +10-15% target.

  The correct mechanism at e5-e7 is NOT per-block bimodal — it is
  Candidate 1 from W44-144: shrink the 2.0/3.0 uniform constants
  (e.g., to 1.5 / 2.5) and accept a smaller SSIM2 win for a smaller
  bytes overhead.

Per-block mechanism MAY still apply at e8+ (W44-105 path):

  At e8+ cjxl IS bimodal. The W44-105 path applies the 4× scale via
  buttloop iter-0 seed (not the W44-109 adaptive_quant pre-scale).
  Routing the W44-105 seed through `w44_145_per_block_qf_scale` could
  hypothetically close the +30% bytes overhead at e8/e9 d=4 while
  preserving the +4 SSIM2 win.

  Not attempted in this chunk (out of scope — W44-145 was specced
  against the e5/e6/e7 W44-109 path). Filed as W44-146+ candidate.

Acceptance gate results:

  (a) SSIM2 budget on terminal d=4: v1 FAIL, v2 PASS
  (b) bytes target on terminal d=4: BOTH FAIL
  (c) adjacent cells: v1 mostly within bfly budget, v2 within all budgets
  (d) terminal e8/e9 d=4: BYTE-IDENTICAL (W44-109 gate doesn't fire at e>=8)
  (e) codec_wiki cells: byte-identical at e8 d=3, small SSIM2 wins at d=4
  (f) terminal d=1.0: byte-identical; d=2: small SSIM2 deltas within budget
  (g) photo cells: ALL 8 BYTE-IDENTICAL
  (h) imac_g3 d=2/d=3: bytes -1.7% to -1.9% (v1), SSIM2 +0.06 to -0.08 (within ±0.10)
  (i) Hash-locks: 36/36 BYTE-IDENTICAL (synthetic fixtures don't trigger gate)
  (j) Multi-decoder roundtrip: not run (mechanism reverted before this gate)

DECISION: HONEST-STOP per task spec ("If the implementation doesn't
close the cluster within the SSIM2/bytes budget: HONEST-STOP, document.
Don't ship a regression").

PRODUCTION STATE:
  - `vardct/butteraugli_loop.rs`: ADDED `w44_145_per_block_qf_scale`
    and `per_block_mask1x1_mean` helpers + 7 unit tests. Both marked
    `#[allow(dead_code)]`. Constants W44_145_PER_BLOCK_MASK_LOW=70.0,
    W44_145_PER_BLOCK_MASK_HIGH=99.5.
  - `vardct/encoder.rs`: qf_pre_scale apply site UNCHANGED in net
    semantics — uniform multiply (pre-W44-145 behaviour). Added an
    explanatory comment block citing this investigation.
  - `jxl-encoder/examples/w44_145_per_block_qac_ab.rs`: A/B harness
    registered in Cargo.toml. The example reads
    `JXL_W44_145_PER_BLOCK_DISABLE` but the production path no longer
